{"id":"retired-measures","title":"Measures the City stopped publishing","question":"Which measures carried a target in the 2019 budget book and are no longer in the City's performance data, and were they on course when last printed?","finding":"The Mayor's budget book for fiscal years 2020 and 2021 printed targets for 127 measures in the departments that fund most nonprofit services. 61 of them (48%) no longer appear under the same name in the Controller's performance dataset. For 15 of those, the department's own projection for fiscal year 2019 was already below that year's target when the book was printed.","how":"Each measure in the performance tables of the Mayor's Proposed Budget for fiscal years 2019-20 and 2020-21 (homelessness, public health, human services, children and youth, early childhood, economic and workforce development, and the Mayor's office including housing) was looked up by name in today's Citywide Performance Metrics dataset. Those not found are listed with the 2017-18 result, the 2018-19 target and the department's projection as printed.","limits":"A measure can vanish because it was renamed, merged or replaced by a better one, not because it was missed: the homelessness department replaced its whole set in fiscal year 2023, and matching is by name only, so a reworded measure counts as retired. Whether a projection below target is bad depends on the measure; for some, such as waiting times or caseloads, lower is better, and no direction is judged here. Later budget books print no performance tables.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"department","t":"Department","type":"text"},{"k":"measure","t":"Measure","type":"text"},{"k":"actual2018","t":"Result 2017-18","type":"text"},{"k":"target2019","t":"Target 2018-19","type":"text"},{"k":"projected2019","t":"Projected 2018-19","type":"text"},{"k":"target2020","t":"Target 2019-20","type":"text"},{"k":"projectedBelowTarget","t":"Projection below target","type":"text"},{"k":"link","t":"Source","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"department":"Economic and Workforce Development","measure":"Number of businesses receiving one-on-one technical assistance","actual2018":"2,165","target2019":"2,500","projected2019":"2,100","target2020":"2,100","projectedBelowTarget":"Yes","link":{"t":"page 180","u":"https://sfbos.org/sites/default/files/Mayor_Proposed_Budget.pdf"}},{"department":"Homelessness and Supportive Housing","measure":"Percent of case managed families in shelters that are placed in permanent or transitional housing, enter a treatment program, or reunite with family","actual2018":"42%","target2019":"65%","projected2019":"60%","target2020":"65%","projectedBelowTarget":"Yes","link":{"t":"page 222","u":"https://sfbos.org/sites/default/files/Mayor_Proposed_Budget.pdf"}},{"department":"Homelessness and Supportive Housing","measure":"Number of individuals reunited with family or friends through the Homeward Bound program***","actual2018":"838","target2019":"850","projected2019":"500","target2020":"850","projectedBelowTarget":"Yes","link":{"t":"page 222","u":"https://sfbos.org/sites/default/files/Mayor_Proposed_Budget.pdf"}},{"department":"Homelessness and Supportive Housing","measure":"Number of individual adults leaving homelessness due to rapid rehousing rental subsidy**","actual2018":"46","target2019":"150","projected2019":"25","target2020":"150","projectedBelowTarget":"Yes","link":{"t":"page 222","u":"https://sfbos.org/sites/default/files/Mayor_Proposed_Budget.pdf"}},{"department":"Human Services","measure":"Percent of children ages 0 to 5 enrolled in City-funded high quality ECE programs","actual2018":"27.3%","target2019":"30.0%","projected2019":"29.7%","target2020":"30.0%","projectedBelowTarget":"Yes","link":{"t":"page 240","u":"https://sfbos.org/sites/default/files/Mayor_Proposed_Budget.pdf"}},{"department":"Human Services","measure":"CLF: Number of unduplicated clients served by the Community Living Fund program in the past six months","actual2018":"416","target2019":"425